💡 Project 2
Evolution of Marine Bioluminescence
🔬 Research Question
How has bioluminescence evolved across marine organisms, and what genetic and regulatory mechanisms control light production?

🌊 Motivation
Bioluminescence is one of the most widespread and remarkable traits in the marine environment. Light-producing systems have evolved independently across multiple lineages including fish, squid, jellyfish, crustaceans and plankton. The repeated evolution of bioluminescence presents an opportunity to investigate how genomes, gene regulatory networks and environmental pressures generate complex biological traits.
This project explores marine bioluminescence through literature review, bioinformatics and computational analysis.

