❓ Key Research Questions
Evolution
How many times has bioluminescence evolved independently in marine organisms?

Genetics
Which genes are associated with bioluminescent systems and how do they vary between species?

Gene Regulation
What mechanisms regulate the timing and location of light production?

Neuroscience
How do nervous systems interact with light-producing cells to create bioluminescent behaviours?

Ecology
What environmental pressures drive the evolution and maintenance of bioluminescence?

🐟 Example Organisms
Dinoflagellates
Microscopic marine plankton responsible for many coastal bioluminescent events.

Firefly Squid
A cephalopod with highly specialised light-producing organs.

Lanternfish
One of the most abundant groups of deep-sea bioluminescent fish.

Copepods
Small crustaceans that use bioluminescence for defence and communication.

Jellyfish
Important models for understanding the evolution of marine light-producing systems.

